From ac2c1ee2a0324f91be389fcae3ad89c30ffdbce7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: skornuta <126527569+skornuta@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 22:17:17 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 13/27] Allocator trim (VICTORY_ALLOCATOR_TRIM=1, off): command
 allocators taken anew

A D3D12 command allocator keeps the memory of the most its list ever
recorded into it. The ~1,600 host lists and preludes of a run held about
2.3 GB of private memory beside the commit the card's memory takes (the
memory minute's residual; 300 allocators of 4,000 commands each took
459 MB on the RTX 5080).

With the switch a host list's reset, and a prelude's before it records
again (the only moments an allocator holds nothing that runs), takes a
new allocator when the one it has is VICTORY_ALLOCATOR_TRIM_S seconds old
(30); the old one goes behind the submissions still running (`retire`),
never while a list could run from it. A title list executed again without
a reset keeps its allocator: only resets swap. Idle pooled lists not
taken for that long are destroyed too (VICTORY_LIST_POOL_IDLE_S takes
the same time when it is not set).

The memory CSV gets the allocators renewed (lists, preludes) and the idle
lists destroyed.

(cherry picked from commit cd5ae448e3c8a4ae713f32291970138407826813)
